  "files": [
    {
      "section": "Clinical Analysis",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 25 trust",
      "description": "Imaging test for this Operator showed blurry outline of internal organs with visible unusual dark spots. Unusually high concentration of Originium particles were present in her circulation, indicating signs of infection and confirming her as infected at this stage. \n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 1%\nSurveillance is recommended for rare cases like this. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.14u/L \nMinor infection currently showing no sign of spreading."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 1",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 50 trust",
      "description": "A freeform fighter.\nShe's the simple, easily fulfilled eat-sleep-repeat type. \nShe enjoys dried fish and honey. So much so, that if offered a compensation package with only those two items, she would actually mull it over."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 2",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 100 trust",
      "description": "Since her underground fighting circuit broke up and everyone involved went into hiding, Rhodes Island has had a hard time gathering records of her past. \nBeehunter doesn't remember her own childhood well. All she knows for certain is she's been making a living off underground fights since a very young age. \nHer ideals come from the underground fighting lifestyle: Live simply, be rude when you have to, solve problems with your fists, and live in the moment."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 3",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 150 trust",
      "description": "There are no rules in underground fights. Winning is all that matters. \nWhen fighting one-on-one, Beehunter can beat most opponents on talent alone. \nHowever, on the battlefield, we rarely have the luxury of a one-on-one fight. Certainly not one with no interference. In short, Beehunter's skillset is not well suited to Rhodes Island's work."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 4",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 200 trust",
      "description": "But Rhodes Island doesn't turn down such talent due to combat capabilities alone. Beehunter's... simplicity left her drill instructor baffled during her onboarding. \nIn the end, we decided to focus on her strengths: Take her opponents one at a time and knock them down as fast as possible. \nShe quite likes this tactic because she doesn't need to think. Still, she does need to learn to observe the flow of battle."
    }
  ]
}
